 intriguing and mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:11:47-07:00","id":718904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves?p=718677#post718677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm probably missing something here, but damned if I don't think it sounds intriguing and mysterious.</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically, the sourcebook Splintered Cities: Seattle establishes that in the city of the same name( D:tD's &quot;corebook setting&quot;) a pocket dimension of 1999 Seattle contains a vault that might be the most guarded piece of Infrastructure in the city. Unbeknownst to the Unchained, this is because the Vault is where the GM stores all the timelines that must never occur... and by that, I mean timelines in which humanity or the planet are destroyed beyond repair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:27:53-07:00","id":719016,"title":"","content":"It's literally called the Apocalypse Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:35:44-07:00","id":719038,"title":"","content":"Damn, I should get that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:16:54-07:00","id":719560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves?p=718904#post718904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Basically, the sourcebook Splintered Cities: Seattle establishes that in the city of the same name( D:tD's &quot;corebook setting&quot;) a pocket dimension of 1999 Seattle contains a vault that might be the most guarded piece of Infrastructure in the city. Unbeknownst to the Unchained, this is because the Vault is where the GM stores all the timelines that must never occur... and by that, I mean timelines in which humanity or the planet are destroyed beyond repair.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Lodge of the Final Winter is a group of werewolves that are attempting to avert the apocalypse better known as &quot;Hey, remember Majora's Mask?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:31:26-07:00","id":719618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves#post714451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a werewolf game. Recently, a loved NPC died, and the pack decided that they wanted to try and resurrect him.<br /> <br /> Half the group being <i>Supernatural</i> fans, I jumped at the chance to bring in some demonic goodness. So they asked around the Shadow, consulting spirits of health and medicine and even death, and heard rumors of a creature known as Mr. Onyx down in Houston who can supposedly bring people back to life &quot;For a price&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo what would an Unchained want from a pack of out-of-town werewolves? A Soul Pact wouldn't be worth the effort since the PCs are all Uratha. I don't think a signatory can promise other characters as cultists, and it wouldn't be too helpful anyway since all of the packmates live a five hour drive away.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think most people have listed great ideas, but there is one option related to your musings above that people generally miss. Remember that you could always just go *BAM* I have a cult. But Sanctity of Merits says that the person you make the leader can flip you off and walk away with your sandbox and all the toys. HOWEVER, if you give free pacts to help people that will be grateful and definitely be useful to you later, that is a &quot;hard way&quot; of building a cult which doesn't tie people to you with anything but loyalty. Then you can raise a cult that can't just walk away from you as it's actually tied to you.<br /> <br /> ** You want your friend brought back. It will be hard, but I can try. If it works, I could also make sure each of you are a little **<br /> ** better prepared to [dodge/soak/parry/etc] so it would be harder for this to happen again. No no, keep your money. That's **<br /> ** not why I do these things. What I need are people I can count on when I'm in trouble. So what you think? Do we have a **<br /> ** deal? **<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves#post714451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Task might be more likely (after all, a pack of werewolves can destroy quite a bit of Infrastructure if they try), but it lacks the &quot;oomph&quot; that I'm hoping will dissuade them from wanting to ever commission Mr. Onyx's services again. I'm guessing Cover details, like parents, exes, the usual.<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe Mr. Onyx will give them a relatively cheap first deal. To get them hooked and all.<br /> <br /> Mostly I'm just looking for ideas (and plausible Pact ideas).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now this is a different situation entirely. You could use the example I gave above with a twist.<br /> <br /> ** Your friend will wake up in a few hours. Yes it took a long time but that was hard work. You didn't say she died last week. **<br /> ** When she wakes, a portion of her being will belong to me. Would you rather I remove the only spark which allows her to **<br /> ** live again? I thought not. She will need to sign in blood before you leave...unless one of you would like to sign for her? **<br /> <br /> Now that same Demon isn't looking for a cult to help them, but is looking to leverage a resurrection into a Soul Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":2668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","user":"Asmenedas","date":".  Formatting correction 10-23-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T11:19:56-07:00","id":719942,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Demons have their Agendas, too, so that could also serve as a possible source to determine &quot;what does Mr. Onyx want?&quot; For example, a Saboteur may be willing to resurrect their friend in exchange for their help in striking against the God-Machine; hunting down and killing GM cultists, assaulting Infrastructure, etc. An Inquisitor may demand information that only werewolves can provide - what are they willing to tell him about the Gauntlet, the Shadow, the ecology of spirits, or even the history and/or powers of werewolves themselves, in exchange for his help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T11:55:10-07:00","id":720039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmenedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves?p=719618#post719618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now this is a different situation entirely. You could use the example I gave above with a twist.<br /> <br /> ** Your friend will wake up in a few hours. Yes it took a long time but that was hard work. You didn't say she died last week. **<br /> ** When she wakes, a portion of her being will belong to me. Would you rather I remove the only spark which allows her to **<br /> ** live again? I thought not. She will need to sign in blood before you leave...unless one of you would like to sign for her? **<br /> <br /> Now that same Demon isn't looking for a cult to help them, but is looking to leverage a resurrection into a Soul Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the NPC is an Uratha as well (from a Pure pack no less: my players are so progressive!), so that'd be an equally difficult Soul Pact to collect on.<br /> <br /> Regarding Cult Pacts, I thought that the signatories were more loyal than that, and I certainly wouldn't want them to relocate to Houston. That being said, &quot;A favor, sometime in the future&quot; is a good one because if the Pact is ever destroyed then the friend will just die again. Like my own little Sword of Damocles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T14:36:52-07:00","id":720610,"title":"","content":"Remember also that Demons aren't tied down to territory. Mr. Onyx might stop by the PC's territory for a visit/business proposal/favor/relocation some time in the future, if it serves.<br /> <br /> All the better if he ends up bringing &quot;heat&quot; with/after him. And <i>then</i> they find out about the unstated consequences if Mr. Onyx (and thus, the Pact) get destroyed before the terms are fulfilled...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T17:42:10-07:00","id":733515,"title":"","content":"He gives them some task to perform that unbeknownst to them draws the GM's attention to them, drawing off its resources to hunt them, leaving Mr. Onyx free to exploit its distraction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:02:15-07:00","id":733557,"title":"","content":"Demon's can make Pacts with supernaturals: that's seems to be a given, considering the consequences for supernatural Soul Pacts is spelled out. Though all the wording lists &quot;mortal&quot; or &quot;human&quot;.<br /> <br /> Considering that, might the werewolves broker a Cult Pact between the Demon and a Spirit (or group of Spirits)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:43:30-07:00","id":733616,"title":"","content":"How well can wolves hand Angels? If a Werewolf can touch and kill Angels, then that's a powerful combatant ally. Offer a few anti-Wound Gadgets (maybe a Near-Field Rip the Gates Gadget that closes Wounds?), maybe some helpful contacts, and you could have a very profitable partnership. Especially if the GM has been screwing the Shadow Ecology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T21:44:35-07:00","id":733899,"title":"","content":"Regarding some issues of the demon's Cover:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=733614#post733614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, depends what they hear.<br /> <br /> if it's &quot;There's a robo-demon who will resurrect people. He lives here, and he takes such-and-such as payment,&quot; then there's a problem.<br /> <br /> If it's more like, &quot;I heard from a guy who heard from a packmate who heard from a cousin who heard on a message board that there's this shady guy who'll bring people back from the dead. Nobody knows where he lives or what he wants, but he says the guy has a red right hand,&quot; then it's still a compromise, but a much smaller one.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how specific the information is, and how much it spreads.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rumor that they heard was from a spirit of health talking about &quot;Something in Houston that's said to be able to grant wishes, supposedly known as 'Mr. Onyx'.&quot;<br /> <br /> The occultist of the group did some research, and I said that there are very few entities in the world capable of bringing people back to life: Powerful sorcerers, high-ranking spirits (and the Health Spirit would have mentioned that), or angels/fallen angels. The group figured that it was either a sorcerer or a fallen angel. I figure the unchained won't have to make a Compromise check until they meet the Cover that he presents to them, so maybe it'll be a burner Cover and he'll act through intermediaries or proxies until he can be sure that the PC werewolves will be capable of delivering on their part of the bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:05:38-07:00","id":734365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves?p=714630#post714630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, Spirits can teach Uratha Gifts. Could an Angel teach an Uratha Embeds? Or, at least, Gifts resembling Embeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don't teach Gifts to Uratha, they literally carve them into werewolves on both the physical and spiritual level\u200bs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:47:06-07:00","id":734710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves?p=734365#post734365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits don't teach Gifts to Uratha, they literally carve them into werewolves on both the physical and spiritual level\u200bs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but &quot;teach&quot; is a lot faster to type, and it gets the point of what I'm saying across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}